---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TesseractHero from '../components/TesseractHero.astro';
import '../styles/company.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Chudware" description="Why Chudware combines exact parametric CAD, manufacturing, simulation, product data, reverse engineering, and an AI copilot in one engineering workspace.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Engineering work should remain connected to the model that produced it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Chudware is dimension-driven parametric CAD for engineers whose work crosses design, analysis, manufacturing, electronics, and product data. Exact solids, ordered features, assemblies, CAM, simulation, reverse engineering, and a team of AI agents all live in one environment.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-why">
    <div class="wrap co-about-body">
      <div class="co-prose">
        <h2 id="co-why" class="co-anchor">Why it exists</h2>
        <p>One design decision usually touches several tools: the CAD model, a simulation setup, a CAM program, a supplier PDF, and a revision record. Chudware keeps all of that attached to one project so the geometry and the evidence for it can be reviewed together.</p>
        <p>The modeling core uses exact boundary-representation solids. Models are dimension-driven: named relations and driving dimensions in fully defined sketches feed an ordered feature tree, and every feature stays human-editable rather than being flattened into a display mesh.</p>

        <h2>Files and delivery</h2>
        <p>The native <code>.step+</code> container keeps the neutral STEP body alongside Chudware feature, parameter, material, study, drawing, and integrity data. The STEP payload can be extracted or exported for exchange even when another system cannot read Chudware's feature history.</p>
        <p>The browser workspace and the desktop app are the same product. Signed x86-64 builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS are on the <a class="text-link" href="https://app.chudware.com/#downloads">account download page</a>.</p>

        <h2>Open-source meshing</h2>
        <p>Chudware builds a pinned revision of the BSD-3-Clause <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Hunter-124/Polyhedral-FEA">PolyMesh project</a> into its FEA meshing path. Chudware owns study setup, resource admission, result packaging, and its engine solvers; the public PolyMesh repository independently includes its mesher, linear-elastostatics solver, validation material, CLI, and study applications. <a class="text-link" href="/open-source/">Read the integration boundary</a>.</p>

        <h2>Commercial preview</h2>
        <p>Chudware is in commercial preview. Core workflows are ready; advanced capabilities and packaging are still changing. Use the 14-day trial on representative files, studies, and CAM handoffs before moving production work.</p>

        <p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hunter-edmonds/" rel="me">Hunter Edmonds on LinkedIn</a></p>
      </div>

      <aside class="co-aside" aria-labelledby="co-posture">
        <TesseractHero />
        <p class="eyebrow" id="co-posture">Engineering principles</p>
        <ol class="co-tenets">
          <li><h3>Keep geometry exact</h3><p>Features operate on B-rep solids; meshes are used where a mesh is the correct representation.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Keep results inspectable</h3><p>Feature history, study setup, mesh evidence, and revisions remain available for review.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Keep physical actions deliberate</h3><p>Toolpaths and machine output require explicit engineering and operator review.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Keep an exchange path</h3><p>Neutral geometry and documented exports prevent a project from depending on one opaque file.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Understand the limits</h3><p>Review preview status, solver assumptions, and supported workflows before committing a project.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-evaluate">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate the product</p>
        <h2 id="co-evaluate" class="co-anchor">Evaluate it on a project that looks like yours.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Compare worked examples with your requirements, follow the workflow guides, and review security controls before introducing restricted project data.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="co-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with evidence</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/gallery/">Gallery</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Documentation</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Changelog</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/security/">Security</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate Chudware</p>
      <h2>Open it in the browser, or install the desktop app.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Start the trial, then test the workflows that matter to you.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/gallery/">View worked examples</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
